319. ~~**/console throws a React hydration error (#418)**~~ — **found and fixed 2026-11-20** (repo `bcf65ba`, checker `ca484d1`):
    root cause was **not** time, locale or randomness. `SiweStub` read `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SIWE_ENABLED` in a client
    module: Next inlines `NEXT_PUBLIC_` only when it is set at build time, while `@opennextjs/cloudflare` copies the Worker's
    request-time variables onto `process.env` for the server — so SSR rendered the enabled branch and the browser evaluated a
    `process` shim and rendered the fallback. Reproduced by building without the var and starting with it set (`next start`
    then logs the same #418), which is why a local build of the same commit never showed it. Fixed by resolving the value on
    the server and passing it as a prop; `ChainTicker` had the same shape with its endpoint and is fixed the same way.
    **Two guards**: `check-client-env.mjs` fails when any client module reads `process.env` (shown failing with the read put
    back), and `check-env-vars.mjs` now scans `.tsx` — its old `ts|mjs|js` filter is why the read was invisible.
    - deployment is the last test: the console redeploy carries the fix; the guard prevents the next one.
    - original scope follows. - found 2026-11-19 by `page-audit`, which now listens for console errors on every route. The server-rendered
    markup and the client's first render disagree on some text; React logs it once and recovers, so a visitor sees a normal page and nothing else noticed.
    - the route is the console; the components on it mix server-rendered timestamps with client components that compute relative time (`ProgressStrip`, `SettledStrip`)
    - **re-tried 2026-11-19 18:30Z, and the reproduction is the blocker.** It reproduces on the deployed site (React #418, args `text`) and **not** on a local
      `next build && next start` of the same commit — so bisecting components locally cannot find it. Two more candidates examined and ruled out on the way:
      Cloudflare HTML rewriting (no `rocket-loader`, no `/cdn-cgi/` scripts, no email-decode in the served HTML) and `Date.now()` during render in a client
      component (the only two are `SettledStrip`, which returns `null` on first render, and `siwe/client.ts`, which runs in a handler).
      Next step is to reproduce on the deployed serving stack (`opennextjs-cloudflare` / `wrangler dev`) rather than on `next start`, because the difference
      between those two runtimes is now the leading suspect.
    - ruled out on 2026-11-19 by reading the components on that route: `SettledStrip` renders `null` until its fetch resolves, so it contributes no server text;
      `StatusStrip` formats with `toUTCString()`, which is timezone-independent; `ProgressStrip.relativeDate` runs in a server component whose HTML the client does not
      re-render. What remains is a client component on `/console` that renders something time- or randomness-dependent on its very first render
    - also ruled out on the same day: six `toLocaleString()` calls with **no locale** in `ChartStrip`, `FunnelPanel` and `ChainTicker` — the classic hydration bug, since
