### Done — 2026-11-17, mcp.so listing could not start the server (#263, `@paystage/mcp@0.8.10`)

Reported by the operator from https://mcp.so/servers/paystage-6d8a8f: `MCP error -32000: Connection closed`
plus an npm log footer, and five tools listed.

**Cause, reproduced in one command:** `npx -y @paystage/mcp` → `npm error could not determine executable
to run`. The package declares four bins and none was named `mcp`, so npm could not pick one; the process
exited before speaking MCP, which is what the client reports as a closed connection. The five tools were
that directory's cache from `0.3.5`, which registered five — a second symptom of never having started.

**Fixed:** an `mcp` alias bin alongside `paystage-mcp`; `scripts/check-bins.mjs` in CI fails any multi-bin
package with no name-matching bin; changelog entry; 0.8.10 published by tag, verified by speaking MCP to
the bare command from a cold cache — **9 tools, stderr null**.

**Lesson:** the README's correct form was `npx -y -p @paystage/mcp paystage-mcp`, and everyone who
generates a config from metadata uses the bare form instead. A correct instruction does not protect you
from the instruction other people write.


